    <string name="ced_help">How it works</string>
    <string name="ced_help_body">• Tap a line to type in it. Enter starts a new line in the same list style.\n• Tap the left margin of lines to select several, then tap a style: it applies to all selected lines.\n• Title names the chapter. Subtitle starts a section. Sub-subtitle starts a classification card. Heading 3 and deeper (use Indent on a heading) structure a classification.\n• Bullets, numbering and letters nest with Indent / Outdent, as deep as you need.\n• Paste recognises -, •, 1., a) and indentation; tab-separated lines become a table.\n• Tables: one row per line, cells separated by |.</string>
    <string name="ced_paste_hint">Lists (-, •, 1., a)) and indentation are recognised. You can restyle any line afterwards.</string>
